WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.868
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.701
You're here. You made it.

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:07.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.734
Well, guys, today is Thursday,

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:11.901
and the star of "Wednesday,"
Jenna Ortega is here.

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:15.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:18.334
You can see her new movie,
"Scream VI," on Friday.

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:20.501
And this weekend, she's hosting
"Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:22.033
which runs into Sunday.

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.868
Right now, Monday is like,
"Did I do something?"

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:25.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:27.467
Let's get to some news here.
Former president Trump is

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:30.968
releasing a book called "Letters
to Trump" that's made up of

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:34.367
150 private letters sent to him
by big-name celebrities

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.734
like Oprah, the Clintons,
and Liza Minnelli.

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:38.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:40.934
It's kind of strange.
Trump is bragging like,

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:42.767
"Look at all the friends
I used to have."

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:44.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:45.467
"It's all in the book."

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:47.501
Yep, the first five letters are
from celebrities,

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.367
the rest are just fan mail from
Scott Baio.

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.200
If the book does well,
the next volume will be

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.767
a collection of
his favorite subpoenas.

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:55.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:57.667
"This is a good one.
This is a great one.

00:00:57.667 --> 00:00:59.300
I love that."

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.300
Here's the cover of the new
book. Look at the cover. Yeah.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.934
"Letters to Trump."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:06.968
That's right.
That's a picture of Trump

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:11.167
writing a letter to himself.

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:13.234
It's letters "to" --
Ah, forget it.

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:15.601
I would like to see the letters
that Trump wrote.

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.601
It's like, "My dearest
Colonel Sanders,

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:19.968
I can't wait to meet you."

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:23.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.801 --> 00:01:27.300
"Meeting you would be the top
thing on my bucket list.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.868
L-O-L.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:30.467
L-O-L.

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:34.367
Switching gears, this year the
Oscars is actually going up

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:36.634
against the season finale of
"The Last of Us."

00:01:36.634 --> 00:01:38.200
[ Audience oohs ]

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.667
Yeah, the Oscars producers must
be worried about ratings because

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:43.234
this is the promo they just
released. Look at this.

00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:47.367
-This Sunday, the stars come out
for the 95th Oscars.

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:49.400
And if you're thinking of
watching "The Last of Us"

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.801
to find out what happens
on the season finale,

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:53.534
well, you don't have to.

00:01:53.534 --> 00:01:54.868
Joel dies.

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:55.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:58.434
The Oscars, where the magic
happens.

00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:00.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Wow.

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:01.834
-No reason to watch.
-Wow.

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:04.400
-Don't worry about it.
Don't worry about it.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.667
Watch the Oscars.

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:08.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:11.734
Did you guys see this?
The WWE is in talks with

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:15.467
multiple states about legalizing
betting on scripted matches.

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.200
Yep, betting on scripted
matches.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.767
What could possibly go right?

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:22.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.167
If you're going to bet on
a sport that's scripted,

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:25.634
bet on boxing.

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:26.701
[ Audience oohs ]

00:02:26.701 --> 00:02:28.200
Hey. Come on.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:31.601
-Wow.
-You guys said it.

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:33.200
I didn't say it.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.200
Guys, listen to this, Spotify
just announced

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.567
that it is focusing on
video podcasts.

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:40.534
Yep. Video podcasts.

00:02:40.534 --> 00:02:42.901
And there's some pretty
interesting ads. Check this out.

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:46.400
-We all love podcasts, but now,
imagine if that podcast

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.667
interview was on television with
lights and hair and makeup

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:54.367
and music and a desk
and a chair and a host.

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:55.534
-♪ Hey, hey-hey ♪

00:02:55.534 --> 00:02:58.167
-"The Tonight Show,"
a podcast you can see.

00:02:58.167 --> 00:02:59.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:00.901
-Wait, we're doing it?

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:02.501
That's what we're doing.

00:03:02.501 --> 00:03:06.400
It's a podcast you can see! Yes!

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:12.434
Well, this is crazy.
NASA is warning that an asteroid

00:03:12.434 --> 00:03:16.033
could hit Earth on
Valentine's Day in 2046.

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:17.434
[ Man cheers ]
No.

00:03:17.434 --> 00:03:18.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:21.400
No. No, I don't --
I don't want to --

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.300
-What is going on?
-Terrible news.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:26.968
That is actually terrible news.

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:28.801
Not a "whoo!" It's a "ooh."

00:03:28.801 --> 00:03:30.901
-It's gonna hit Earth, yay!

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:33.701
-But believe it or not, Hallmark
is already selling special

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:35.534
Valentine's Day cards
for the big day.

00:03:35.534 --> 00:03:36.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:38.300
Yeah, check these out.
The first card says...

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:40.901
You open it up, it says...

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:44.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.901 --> 00:03:46.234
This next card says...

00:03:47.434 --> 00:03:48.434
You open it up, it says...

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:53.133
The next card says...

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:55.801
Open it up, it says...

00:03:59.701 --> 00:04:01.167
And finally, this last card
says...

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:03.667
Open it up, it says...

00:04:04.934 --> 00:04:06.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:08.100
Sweet. Really nice.

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:15.133
Hey, I read that the TSA is
ordering airports to step up

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:16.734
their cybersecurity.

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:19.100
Airports are like, "Yeah, we'll
get on that right after

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:23.000
we figure out shoes and belts.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.734
Take 'em off. I don't know
what's in --"

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:28.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.367
"We don't -- I don't know
anything about belts.

00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:32.200
Take 'em off.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:35.234
Look at that guy's feet.
That looks suspicious."

00:04:35.234 --> 00:04:37.400
You shouldn't be smoking here.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.367
Meanwhile, JFK Airport is like,

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:41.734
"We have no Wi-Fi, computers,
or electricity.

00:04:41.734 --> 00:04:43.367
How much more secure
can we get?"

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:46.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:50.067
We don't have anything.

00:04:50.067 --> 00:04:53.267
Speaking of travel, a woman said
that Delta Airlines damaged

00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:55.467
her bag during a flight
and agreed to replace it

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:58.067
but then sent her
13 new suitcases.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:00.367
Well, new to her.

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:02.334
They were just 13 suitcases of
other passengers.

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:04.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.067 --> 00:05:06.701
Well, this is going viral.
Maine is trying to get rid of

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:09.400
any inappropriate
license plates. Yeah.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:12.300
But one driver claims that his
plate is being misinterpreted.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:14.968
Watch this.
-A vegan in Maine whose custom

00:05:14.968 --> 00:05:18.734
license plate contains the word
"tofu," is one of the drivers

00:05:18.734 --> 00:05:22.334
caught up in the state crackdown
on vulgar vanity plates.

00:05:22.334 --> 00:05:26.434
This is the plate in question.
It says "luvtofu," but the state

00:05:26.434 --> 00:05:29.200
thinks it could be seen as
an inappropriate reference.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:35.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:38.901
-That person is definitely
not vegan, and that 100% means

00:05:38.901 --> 00:05:40.534
what officials think it means,
okay?

00:05:40.534 --> 00:05:42.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.634 --> 00:05:44.601
And finally, you know, we love
video games here

00:05:44.601 --> 00:05:46.267
at "The Tonight Show" and
we also love movies.

00:05:46.267 --> 00:05:47.501
That's why we're so excited
about

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:49.601
"The Super Mario Bros. Movie"
coming out.

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:52.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

